; A curve reached only AFTER a long stretch of ordinary extrusion, in relative-E (M83) mode.
; The point of this fixture is that stretch: in arc-circle.gcode the weldable curve is the
; very first thing extruded, so the running absolute E and the run’s own relative delta are
; numerically identical and a step that confuses the two looks correct. Every real sliced file
; reaches its curves with hundreds of mm already extruded, which is what this reproduces --
; a shipped defect emitted the absolute total onto the welded arc and no golden caught it.
